description:
FILED s532a (Opus 5.5, 2026-11-01) when #4084 (the BLOCKS table alias) was fixed and chomp.t's 18 other rows passed: rows 21 (winsux2 out) and 25 (winsux4 out) still fail.  PRE-EXISTING (base 10cdc985 renders the same).

    use lib "$ENV{HOME}/.cpan/build/Template-Toolkit-3.106-0/lib"; use Template;
    my $tt = Template->new({ BLOCKS => { w2 => "[% ding -%]\015\012\015\012[% dong %]", w4 => "[% ding %]\015\012\015\012[%- dong %]" } });
    for my $b (qw(w2 w4)) { my $out = ''; $tt->process($b, { ding => 'Hello', dong => 'World' }, \$out);
      $out =~ s/([^\w ])/sprintf('\\%03o', ord $1)/ge; print "$b [$out]\n" }
  perl 5.40.3: w2 [Hello\015\012World] / w4 [Hello\015\012World]
  PCL: w2 [Hello\012World] / w4 [Hello\012World]

NOT the chomp regexes themselves: `s{ ^ ([^\S\n]* \n) }{}x` and `s{ (\r?\n|^) [^\S\n]* \z }{}mx` on the same strings answer as perl (scratch/s532a/p/cr.pl).  winsux1 / winsux3 (one CRLF) pass.  Next: instrument Template::Parser::split_text's $pre / $text around the CHOMP_ALL arms with the double-CRLF input (scratch/s532a/p/tt2.pl in the s532a worktree).
